OOP terms:

class is a blueprint that describes the data structure and methods/functionality of an object

object is a specific instance created from a class 

methods defines what an object can do, which was instantiated from a class

constructors are special class member functions that are used for initializing data of a class

encapsulation is the practice of hiding internal class data and only allowing access to these via public methods like getters and setters

abstraction is the concept of hiding complex implementation to make a simple interface 

composition is when a class has instances of other classes as attributes
for example: we have a class called Point that has an object (x,y), and a city class that contains an object called location that is an instance of Point actually, and through this its possible to store a point (x,y) in location as an attribute

inheritance is when a child/class inherits attirbutes and methods of a base/parent class.

polymorphism is the concept of treating an object of a specific type as various types based on its inheritance hierarchy


